{
  "name": "app-kit",
  "version": "0.5.0",
  "description": "The baseline every app ships with, written once. Its web part: a fetch wrapper that turns a 401 into sign-in over the current address, the server-unreachable line, the new-deploy line, the reload after a failed screen load, an error boundary, links for rows and cards, and a sign-in gate behind a provider adapter, with Clerk the first adapter. Its extension part: self-reload from the checkout, build and account identity, alarms, recorded errors, a native host over a unix socket, and a hidden-Chromium test harness. Its desktop sign-in part: a desktop app's window signs in through the default browser and back, with the account chosen in the window, a nonce only that window matches, and the server routes both ends use.",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "exports": {
    "./web": "./src/index.ts",
    "./web/clerk": "./clerk/index.tsx",
    "./web/testing": "./testing/index.tsx",
